  "notes": [
   "The datasheet E-4021 covers two papers, Portra Endura (low contrast) and Supra Endura (slightly higher contrast); each has its own characteristic-curve plot (page 9). The spectral-dye-density and spectral-sensitivity plots (page 10) are not labelled by paper: the same traced curves are given in both sheets and apply to both papers as printed.",
   "Characteristic curves: x axis is absolute log exposure in lux-seconds as printed (-3.0 to 0.0), plotted from about -1.95 to -0.07; process RA-4 95 F (35 C) 45 seconds, Status A. Exposure time and light source of the curves are not stated, so balance is null.",
   "Characteristic curves: leaders on the plot name R, G and B; the lone curve to the right in the rise ends second highest at the top (about 2.61) and is G, the lowest end (about 2.49) is B, the remaining curve (end about 2.58) is R. G crosses R and B in the shoulder. R and B overlap closely through the toe and rise; the traced lines there follow the centre of the merged ink band and differ by up to about 0.05 density.",
   "Spectral sensitivity: effective exposure 0.5 sec, process RA-4; y is log sensitivity (reciprocal of exposure in erg/cm2 required to produce specified density) as printed; r = cyan-forming layer (drawn 495-740 nm), g = magenta-forming layer (the sheet draws it from 389 nm, starting at 0.0 with a near vertical stroke down to about -0.46 at 395 nm; traced from 395 nm), b = yellow-forming layer (379-510 nm).",
   "Spectral dye density: process RA-4, diffuse spectral density, absolute (not normalised) with x axis 350-700 nm; curves are drawn from 380 nm; yellow peaks at about 450 nm (a shoulder near 420 nm), magenta at 550 nm, cyan at about 635 nm. All three start between 1.3 and 1.45 at 380 nm and the steep first 20 nm overlap; there is no minimum-density or neutral curve.",
   "No grain data, D-min values or log H reference are printed in this sheet."
